# Extraction stub — arXiv:2101.09316 (non-unitary VQE)

**Note:** the arXiv PDF for this paper is a clean Qiskit / LaTeX build with
selectable text; `work/paper.txt` (produced by plain `pdftotext`) is already
high fidelity and was used as the primary machine-readable source for the
claim mapping and Hamiltonian coefficient cross-check. A full Nougat pass
was not needed to reach the REPLICATED verdict; this file exists to record
the intended extraction pipeline and provide a canonical .mmd landing spot
for the QC-100 8-artifact standard.

## Extraction pipeline (canonical)
```
# 1. Primary text (fast, adequate for this paper)
pdftotext -layout work/paper.pdf work/paper.txt

# 2. Optional Nougat pass (deeper equation / table structure)
#    Nougat: Meta Neural Optical Understanding for Academic Documents.
#    Run on uicgpu free A100 slot per compute-priority rule:
#      ssh uicgpu 'cd $STAGING && nougat paper.pdf --out out/ --model 0.1.0-base'
#    Output would land here as extraction/nougat.mmd .
```

## Content actually extracted (via pdftotext) and used
- **Sec. II — Method.** Definitions of the estimator
  `E_nu = <psi|J H J|psi> / <psi|J^2|psi>`, Eq. 10 in the paper.
- **Sec. II.B — Jastrow ansatz.** Form
  `J = exp( sum_k alpha_k Z_k + sum_{k<l} alpha_{kl} Z_k Z_l )`.
- **Sec. V — Numerical results.**
  - Sec. V.A — noiseless H2 / LiH / H2O convergence (used for C1 verification).
  - Sec. V.B — noisy H2 6-31G on ibmq_boeblingen noise model, Figs. 7–8
    (HEADLINE for C2 — the ratio quoted as "one order of magnitude").
- **Table of claims** cross-checked against the pdftotext output and mapped
  into `report/REPORT.md` §1.

## Equations lifted (for the replication code)
- H2 STO-3G / parity+reduction Hamiltonian coefficients — NOT taken from
  this paper's PDF; instead sourced from the primary literature
  O'Malley et al., PRX 6, 031007 (2016), at R=0.7414 Å. This was
  intentional to keep the code build independent of the paper.
- Estimator formula and Jastrow form: lifted directly from the paper
  (Sec. II / Eq. 10). These are the paper's core object being replicated.

